values ('c5d6e7f8-9a0b-4c55-8d45-5e6f7a8b9c75', 'introduction-to-comparative-politics', 'Introduction to Comparative Politics', 'Compare political systems through field scope, the comparative method, concepts, measurement, and causal puzzles. Topics cover the state and state-building, nations and citizenship, democracy and democratic quality, authoritarian and hybrid regimes, constitutions and courts, parliamentary and presidential systems, electoral systems and parties, political culture and media, development and welfare states, political inclusion, protest and regime change, conflict and post-conflict governance, comparative data and research design, and a regional case portfolio.');

